I have completed the exact minimal correction to resolve the React StrictMode ownership bug.

### Changed File: `src/App.jsx`

```javascript
// src/App.jsx
  useEffect(() => {
    const audioManager = getAudioManager(); // Idempotently acquired and attached during setup phase
    const interval = window.setInterval(() => setHud(getHud(gameRef.current)), 100);
    return () => {
       window.clearInterval(interval);
       audioManager.dispose(); // That exact instance handles cleanup
    };
  }, []);
```

### Confirmation
I explicitly confirm that the audio manager is **no longer acquired only during cleanup**. By invoking `getAudioManager()` at the top of the effect's setup closure, the manager implicitly attaches during the React setup lifecycle. When React StrictMode simulates an effect unmount and subsequent remount without re-rendering, `dispose()` is correctly followed by another `getAudioManager()` call in the second effect setup, resolving the detached state bug.

